TI  - Aeration and pH Combined Regulation for the Phase Separation of Anaerobic Digestion
AU  - FU Guang-qing
PY  - 2013
JO  - China Biogas
AB  - To study the influence of the pH and aeration combined regulation on the phase separation of anaerobic digestion,experiments of different initial pH of 5.5,6.5 and 7.5,different aeration interval of 8 h,12 h and 16 h,and different aeration volume of 3 L,5 L and 8 L,were carried out with glucose as substrate,and further more with rice straw as substrate adopting two-phase anaerobic system were evaluated.The results showed that continuous aeration could reduce the pH and elevated the redox potential.When the initial pH was 6,aeration interval was 8h,and the amount of aeration was 5 L,the methane production was obviously suppressed during the anaerobic fermentation with glucose.In the two-phase anaerobic digestion with rice straw,if the liquid of methanogenic phase would not be refluxed to hydrolysis phase,adjusted the initial pH of the hydrolysis phase below 6.5,aerated three times daily at interval of 8h with ≥ 1 L air per L of container volume,the methane production in hydrolysis phase could be effectively suppressed,and achieve the phase separation basically.
